   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Butterflies are fragile creatures that cannot survive long journeys.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Butterflies fly north in March and lay their eggs on milkweed leaves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"People should never start a project they cannot finish themselves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-of-theme"},{"text":"Meaningful work can be shared across many lives, even if no one sees all of it.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Meaningful work can be shared across many lives, even if no one sees all of it.$q$, $q$No single butterfly completes the trip, yet together the generations do, and the speaker applies this to work that "someone else will have to end." The milkweed choice is a fact from the poem, not its message.$q$, 'draft', 'cb146cb0-3216-53e1-887d-2b0f5e020adb')
