   $q$Which statement best expresses the theme of the fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is always a mistake to admire the talents of others in the forest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Trying to be someone else can make you lose sight of the value of who you are.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Foxes are clever animals that can learn to copy the calls of many birds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Animals in the forest should never laugh at a neighbor who is practicing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Trying to be someone else can make you lose sight of the value of who you are.$q$, $q$Sorrel's borrowed voices fail, while the bark she was ashamed of saves the deer. The ending says she still admires the owl and crows, so admiring others is not the mistake.$q$, 'draft', '8a38b6e1-9414-5766-8c8d-d57008b44844')
