  ('9074e542-f849-5238-ad87-1c27bc33413d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-theme-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker describes a father who quits the bakery because customers never thank him for the bread.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"The speaker describes a father who bakes before dawn for a town that never sees his work, comes to see it as meaningful rather than sad, and asks to learn it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker describes a hardworking, wonderful father whose unfair job deserves far more praise than it gets.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"The speaker describes the flour on a baker's sleeves, a clock above a bench, and loaves rising in rows.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker describes a father who bakes before dawn for a town that never sees his work, comes to see it as meaningful rather than sad, and asks to learn it.$q$, $q$The correct summary covers the father's work, the speaker's change of view, and the note. The speaker comes to believe the father "likes it so," so calling the job unfair adds an opinion the poem moves away from.$q$, 'draft', 'e1083313-f281-5516-b4ab-a092af8eabbf')
