   $q$What does the final stanza add to the theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows the speaker hoping to earn the customers' thanks that the father never got.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-theme"},{"text":"It shows the speaker complaining about having to wake up so early in the morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It shows the speaker wants to take over the bakery so the father can stop working.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows the speaker choosing to join the work, so its quiet value is being passed on.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows the speaker choosing to join the work, so its quiet value is being passed on.$q$, $q$The speaker sets a clock for four and writes "Show me how," choosing to learn the father's patient work. The speaker has just decided that thanks are not the point, so seeking customers' thanks goes against the poem's direction.$q$, 'draft', 'e1083313-f281-5516-b4ab-a092af8eabbf')
